Attribution

  Technique
      The logrotate rename-then-create race, discovered and first weaponised
      by Wolfgang Hotwagner in logrotten.
      https://github.com/whotwagner/logrotten
      https://tech.feedyourhead.at/content/abusing-a-race-condition-in-logrotate-to-elevate-privileges

  Canonical real-world instance
      CVE-2019-10143, FreeRADIUS: a radacct log directory owned by the radiusd
      user let a local attacker turn root-run logrotate into an arbitrary
      write. The same class covers CVE-2016-1247 (Dawid Golunski, the Debian
      nginx package).

The MIT grant above covers this implementation: the logslip rewrite in
logslip.c and the write-up. The race condition is not mine; it is Hotwagner's
research, credited in the file header and the README. This is not a
relicensing of logrotten, which carries its own terms.
